{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And when you slaughter a peace-offering to YHWH.</b> When you wish to serve Him in worship, you shall not do so for idols or molten gods, but for the unique Name — this is what it says, לה׳. And 'you shall not do this' on condition to receive a reward, but rather לרצונכם — that is, your intention shall be to do His will alone, and that it be 'acceptable to you.' And concerning what it says, תזבחהו — and not תזבחו — just as it says in the section אמור אל הכהנים: וכי תזבחו זבח תודה לה׳ לרצונכם תזבחו — our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: תזבחהו is written deficient, without a ו״ו, to teach that a person does not slaughter two offerings at once in consecrated animals, but one offering, and not that two persons slaughter one offering. And from the fact that the Merciful One forbade this in consecrated animals, infer from it that in profane animals it is permitted — and this is what we learned: 'One who slaughters two heads at once — his slaughter is valid; two who hold the knife and slaughter' — thus our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded it in tractate חולין." "<b>And it is possible</b> to say by way of the Kabbalah, concerning the addition of the ה״א and the ו״ו in the word תזבחוהו, from what is known: that the two final letters of the unique Name are two attributes, mercy and judgment. And since this verse mentions the offering of שלמים, and the שלמים come to harmonize the attributes, therefore it was necessary to add here these two letters, alluding to the two attributes — in the manner of the addition of the ה״א and ו״א in (Exodus 2:6) ותראהו את הילד, concerning which they said: ותרא should have sufficed for me, and they expounded it to mean that she saw the Shekhinah with him. But there, in the case of the תודה, which is an offering of thanksgiving to the unique Name, it did not mention the letter ה״א, and said תזבחו — and this is clear."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:45.803230060Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}